@startuml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

participant "AI Controller\n(AIC)" as AIC
participant "TMF 915 API\n(MMB Layer)" as MMB
database "Model Catalog\n(AiModelSpecification)" as Catalog
participant "Deployment Orchestrator\n(AIC Node / Docker Host)" as Docker

== 1. Discovery and Evaluation ==
AIC -> MMB: GET /aiModelSpecification\n(Search for specific capability e.g., anomaly-detection)
activate MMB
MMB -> Catalog: Query Catalog
Catalog --> MMB: Return available blueprints & performance metrics
MMB --> AIC: Return Candidate Models
deactivate MMB

== 2. Instantiation Trigger ==
AIC -> AIC: Evaluate metrics & select optimal model
AIC -> MMB: POST /aiModel\n(target: AiModelSpecification, state: "reserved", targetNode: "AIC-Host")
activate MMB

== 3. Localized Deployment Execution ==
note right of MMB
  MMB delegates the deployment process to the target 
  compute node. In this scenario, the AIC itself acts 
  as the Docker host for localized execution.
end note

MMB -> Docker: Instruct container instantiation\n(Pull image & run on AIC Node)
activate Docker
Docker --> Docker: Resolve Artifacts\nCheck Image Cache & Build
Docker --> Docker: Expose Prediction Endpoint (e.g., port 8080)
Docker --> MMB: Confirm bindings & running state
deactivate Docker

== 4. Lifecycle Finalization & Inference Loop ==
MMB -> MMB: Update entity state to ACTIVE
MMB --> AIC: Return 2xx Created\n(Includes localized hostPort/ip mappings)
deactivate MMB

AIC -> AIC: Register active inference endpoint
AIC -> Docker: Send real-time data for prediction (REST / gRPC)
Docker --> AIC: Return AI Inference

@enduml